{# The one non-obvious fact on the site, and the reason this article exists:
   there are no accounts here. A booking is found by session id -- see
   BookingRepository::forSession() -- so the list is the browser's, and the
   reference is the only part of a booking somebody carries away. #}
<h2>The reference is the booking</h2>
<p>
    If you saw a booking reference on the confirmation page, the booking
    exists. The email is a copy of it, not the ticket itself. Write the
    reference down: it is what an airline asks for.
</p>

<h2>The email</h2>
<p>
    It goes to the address you gave at checkout and can take a few minutes to
    arrive. If it has not turned up after that, look in your spam folder.
</p>

<h2>It is on this site too &mdash; in this browser</h2>
<p>
    Every booking you make appears under <a href="/my/bookings">My
    bookings</a>. There are no accounts here, so that list belongs to the
    browser you booked in. Open it on another device, or after clearing your
    browsing data, and it will be empty.
</p>
<p>
    Nothing is lost when that happens and the booking still stands. But the
    reference is the part of it you keep, which is the whole reason to write it
    down.
</p>

<h2>If you gave the wrong address</h2>
<p>
    We cannot send it a second time. Contact the airline with your reference
    and give it the right address.
</p>
